-- title:
--   The pole chart base-changes along a localisation
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field carrying an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ an element assumed nonzero; let $R'$ be a commutative ring that is an $R$-algebra and also an $F$-subalgebra base in the sense that $F$ is an $R'$-algebra compatibly with its $R$-algebra structure, and let $M \subseteq R$ be a submonoid such that $R'$ is a localisation of $R$ at $M$. Write $A_\infty :=$ `chartAlgInf R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[j^{-1}]$ of $F$ generated by $j^{-1}$, i.e. the integral closure of $R[j^{-1}]$ in $F$, and likewise $A'_\infty :=$ `chartAlgInf R' F j` for the integral closure of $R'[j^{-1}]$ in $F$. The assertion is that the commuting square of affine schemes whose two maps out of $\operatorname{Spec} A'_\infty$ are induced by the inclusion $A_\infty \subseteq A'_\infty$ and by the structure map $R' \to A'_\infty$, and whose two maps into $\operatorname{Spec} R$ are induced by $R \to A_\infty$ and by $R \to R'$, is cartesian: $\operatorname{Spec} A'_\infty$ is a fibre product of $\operatorname{Spec} A_\infty$ and $\operatorname{Spec} R'$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the pole chart of the two-chart integral model attached to the pair $(F,j)$ with localisation of the base: the chart over $M^{-1}R$ is the base change of the chart over $R$, reflecting the fact that integral closure commutes with localisation. It is used to produce the pullback squares over localised bases in `exists_isPullback_toBase_of_isLocalization` and the base-change isomorphism in `exists_iso_baseChange_baseChange_of_isLocalization`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_isPullback_chartInf.lean

